WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.165 --> 00:00:00.998
(mouse clicks)

00:00:00.998 --> 00:00:04.230
- [Narrator] In 2021, many people
started searching for KN car,

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:06.450
but there's no car company by that name.

00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:09.630
Turns out, people were
misreading Kia's new logo.

00:00:09.630 --> 00:00:12.660
This change was part of Kia's
multimillion dollar rebrand

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:15.240
in 2021, which included new colors,

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:17.700
redesigned dealerships, and a new website.

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:19.140
- This new logo is absolutely a way

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:21.210
for them to redefine
their competitive set.

00:00:21.210 --> 00:00:22.260
They're no longer competing

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:25.380
with Honda, or Toyota, or Ford, or GM.

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:27.210
They're trying to compete with Tesla.

00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:28.920
- [Narrator] So let's
break down Kia's rebrand

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:31.050
and see how it's using a new logo

00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:33.303
to try to move its brand upmarket.

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:38.100
Kia has been around for almost 80 years

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:39.840
and in that time, the company has gone

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:42.000
through six iterations of its logo.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:44.190
- The history of Kia
really is in manufacturing,

00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:47.010
and you see that with some of
the history of their logos.

00:00:47.010 --> 00:00:48.720
- [Narrator] Blake Howard
is the creative director

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:51.510
of Matchstic, a brand
identity firm in Atlanta.

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:54.840
He's also the host of a podcast
that dissects logo changes.

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:56.253
- And it wasn't really until they went

00:00:56.253 --> 00:00:58.800
into the US car market that
they started to think more

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:03.390
about their own proprietary,
branded vehicles, or product.

00:01:03.390 --> 00:01:05.520
- [Narrator] This logo launched in 1994,

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:08.730
the same year Kia officially
entered the US market.

00:01:08.730 --> 00:01:10.080
- [Narrator 1] Introducing Kia.

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:11.580
- [Narrator] Where it
differentiated itself

00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:14.460
with the price of its
cars, and this reputation

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:18.030
of being a budget brand
stuck along with its logo.

00:01:18.030 --> 00:01:22.240
- Kia, for years, has been
the value brand in the US,

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:25.350
the thing that teens might
get as their first car.

00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:26.700
- [Narrator] Here's
what some consumers said

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:27.533
they thought about Kia.

00:01:27.533 --> 00:01:28.830
- This is the standard car.

00:01:28.830 --> 00:01:30.265
- Value for money product.

00:01:30.265 --> 00:01:31.830
(speaks foreign language)

00:01:31.830 --> 00:01:32.840
- [Narrator] But according to surveys

00:01:32.840 --> 00:01:34.710
by the research firm, J.D. Power,

00:01:34.710 --> 00:01:37.740
the quality of Kia cars has
been improving for years.

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:40.050
- In the early 2000s,
they started to focus more

00:01:40.050 --> 00:01:43.710
on design, car design, the product design

00:01:43.710 --> 00:01:46.320
and in a lot of ways,
the old logo felt like

00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:49.800
it was an eyesore slapped
onto that more modern product

00:01:49.800 --> 00:01:51.120
that they had already produced.

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:53.160
So now with this more modern logo,

00:01:53.160 --> 00:01:55.110
they actually finally feel like the Kia

00:01:55.110 --> 00:01:58.350
that a lot of us maybe
already knew was out there.

00:01:58.350 --> 00:02:00.000
- [Narrator] Kia hopes
to change its brand image

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:03.783
with this 2021 rebrand,
specifically with its new logo.

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:06.270
- So when we think about logo design,

00:02:06.270 --> 00:02:07.620
there are three things
that we think about,

00:02:07.620 --> 00:02:09.270
shape, color, content.

00:02:09.270 --> 00:02:11.460
- [Narrator] And Kia made
changes to all three.

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:14.220
In terms of shape, Kia ditched
the traditional container

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:16.590
that many other car
companies use in their logos.

00:02:16.590 --> 00:02:18.240
- So you can see Honda has a container.

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:20.460
Toyota has traditionally
had that container,

00:02:20.460 --> 00:02:22.440
and that's because it's super functional.

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:24.960
It's easy to slap on that container shape

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:26.490
as a separate piece of artwork

00:02:26.490 --> 00:02:29.250
on any type of make or model of a vehicle

00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:31.920
- [Narrator] For color, Kia
swapped out red for black

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:34.170
to not only indicate a dramatic change

00:02:34.170 --> 00:02:36.540
from its previous logos,
but also to stand out

00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:37.830
from other car brands.

00:02:37.830 --> 00:02:39.810
- Red and blue are the most popular colors

00:02:39.810 --> 00:02:42.300
for brands to choose in the United States,

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:44.370
which is no surprise.

00:02:44.370 --> 00:02:46.740
And when you look in the car
market, you see a lot of red,

00:02:46.740 --> 00:02:49.290
specifically with foreign import brands.

00:02:49.290 --> 00:02:51.120
- [Narrator] Kia also
changed its brand colors

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:53.220
to Midnight Black and Polar White.

00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:55.110
- It's no longer just a generic red,

00:02:55.110 --> 00:02:56.580
it's no longer a generic white.

00:02:56.580 --> 00:02:59.400
Even the nuanced decision
in color like that signals

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:01.290
that they're a little
bit more design-driven.

00:03:01.290 --> 00:03:04.890
Consumers might not generally
recognize it at a high level,

00:03:04.890 --> 00:03:07.320
but I do think it all
starts to feel cohesive,

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:08.760
and it will build a visual language

00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:11.910
for Kia over time that
hopefully is recognizable.

00:03:11.910 --> 00:03:13.920
- [Narrator] Finally, there's
the content of the logo,

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:15.960
which involves the choice of typography.

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:18.060
- It's always ideal to have

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:19.230
the brand name front and center

00:03:19.230 --> 00:03:22.410
out in the marketplace as
loud and proud as possible.

00:03:22.410 --> 00:03:24.660
- [Narrator] And Kia chose
to represent its brand name

00:03:24.660 --> 00:03:25.890
in an abstract way.

00:03:25.890 --> 00:03:28.620
But this design choice
has caused some confusion.

00:03:28.620 --> 00:03:33.620
- Saw this logo on a car and
thought it was nine inch nails.

00:03:33.630 --> 00:03:35.910
- The biggest criticism
is around legibility.

00:03:35.910 --> 00:03:38.460
When people see a car brand,

00:03:38.460 --> 00:03:41.760
they expect to quickly understand
what the brand name is,

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:44.218
especially when there
are letters involved.

00:03:44.218 --> 00:03:45.360
- [Narrator] Blackspace, the agency

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:47.130
that designed Kia's new logo says

00:03:47.130 --> 00:03:49.620
the lettering is meant to
look like a cursive signature.

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:51.390
- They were inspired by calligraphy

00:03:51.390 --> 00:03:54.090
and they were working with
different Korean glyphs

00:03:54.090 --> 00:03:55.620
and the letters are built off

00:03:55.620 --> 00:03:58.260
of consistent parallel angled lines

00:03:58.260 --> 00:04:00.690
that represent this idea of rising.

00:04:00.690 --> 00:04:02.160
- [Narrator] They said the
rising strokes are meant

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:03.900
to symbolize the meaning of Kia,

00:04:03.900 --> 00:04:05.673
which is to come up out of Asia.

00:04:06.630 --> 00:04:08.790
Another big part of
Kia's rebranding effort

00:04:08.790 --> 00:04:11.130
is redesigning its dealerships in the US.

00:04:11.130 --> 00:04:12.900
- The new dealerships are really designed

00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:15.150
to be less like an office space

00:04:15.150 --> 00:04:17.910
and more like a high-end retail outlet

00:04:17.910 --> 00:04:20.220
where the cars are laid out is open

00:04:20.220 --> 00:04:22.380
and spacious and metallic.

00:04:22.380 --> 00:04:23.850
- [Narrator] Kia says it is also trying

00:04:23.850 --> 00:04:25.530
to attract electric vehicle buyers

00:04:25.530 --> 00:04:26.880
who typically don't like going

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:28.860
to traditional car dealerships.

00:04:28.860 --> 00:04:31.080
Kia isn't the only car company investing

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:32.550
in a new dealership look,

00:04:32.550 --> 00:04:34.890
nor is it unique in changing its logo.

00:04:34.890 --> 00:04:37.170
But what may set Kia apart is the speed

00:04:37.170 --> 00:04:39.390
and breadth of its rebranding efforts.

00:04:39.390 --> 00:04:43.170
- This is something that
usually happens slowly

00:04:43.170 --> 00:04:45.900
and surely over a number of
years, and Kia's seem to be,

00:04:45.900 --> 00:04:48.527
by comparison, doing
this at breakneck speed.

00:04:48.527 --> 00:04:49.360
(upbeat music)

00:04:49.360 --> 00:04:51.090
- [Narrator] So how has
Kia's business changed

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:54.300
since it unveiled its
rebrand In January, 2021?

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:56.790
- Clearly Kia's on a roll.

00:04:56.790 --> 00:04:59.730
They had their best to
ever third quarter recently

00:04:59.730 --> 00:05:00.780
in terms of sales in the US.

00:05:00.780 --> 00:05:03.900
- [Narrator] Kia's
revenue shot up in 2021,

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:06.030
and this year it launched the EV6,

00:05:06.030 --> 00:05:08.190
the company's first dedicated EV model

00:05:08.190 --> 00:05:11.430
and the Niro EV, both with
a starting US sticker price

00:05:11.430 --> 00:05:13.440
of around $40,000.

00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:17.790
Kia says it plans to release
14 EV models globally by 2027,

00:05:17.790 --> 00:05:19.920
and it plans to sell 1.2 million

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:22.230
electric vehicles a year by 2030.

00:05:22.230 --> 00:05:24.660
- And that puts them well in the running

00:05:24.660 --> 00:05:27.810
for among the top EV sellers in the world.

00:05:27.810 --> 00:05:29.220
- [Narrator] But the
inflation reduction act,

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:30.330
which passed in August,

00:05:30.330 --> 00:05:33.300
could throw a wrench in
Kia's ambitious plans.

00:05:33.300 --> 00:05:35.580
The new law requires cars to be assembled

00:05:35.580 --> 00:05:37.440
in the US in order to qualify

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:40.710
for the government's $7,500 EV tax credit.

00:05:40.710 --> 00:05:42.780
Kia and its sister company, Hyundai Motor

00:05:42.780 --> 00:05:45.570
have factories in the US
for their gas-powered cars.

00:05:45.570 --> 00:05:48.450
But their EVs are currently made in Korea.

00:05:48.450 --> 00:05:51.720
Hyundai's $5.5 billion
EV and battery factory

00:05:51.720 --> 00:05:54.750
in Georgia is only set to open in 2025.

00:05:54.750 --> 00:05:57.360
- South Korea and the US
are currently in talks

00:05:57.360 --> 00:06:01.140
about possibly figuring out
a way around this problem.

00:06:01.140 --> 00:06:06.120
But if things don't change,
Kia could face a huge challenge

00:06:06.120 --> 00:06:08.913
in reaching its sales target for 2030.

00:06:09.960 --> 00:06:11.610
- [Narrator] The other
big challenge facing Kia

00:06:11.610 --> 00:06:13.530
is that almost every major car maker

00:06:13.530 --> 00:06:15.630
is coming out with EVs at the same time.

00:06:15.630 --> 00:06:17.760
- Every time that happens,
whether it's a pickup truck,

00:06:17.760 --> 00:06:20.790
a minivan, a hatchback, or a
new battery-powered vehicle,

00:06:20.790 --> 00:06:22.320
the challenge for these companies

00:06:22.320 --> 00:06:25.860
is always how to stand out
in those crowded spaces.

00:06:25.860 --> 00:06:27.210
- [Narrator] With all
the changes it's made

00:06:27.210 --> 00:06:29.970
over the last two years,
Kia is not only betting big

00:06:29.970 --> 00:06:32.040
on the EV boom, but it's also banking

00:06:32.040 --> 00:06:34.920
on the lasting ripple effects
of its rebranding efforts.

00:06:34.920 --> 00:06:37.770
- Branding really is a
long-term investment.

00:06:37.770 --> 00:06:40.410
It's redefining these micro-touch points

00:06:40.410 --> 00:06:42.240
that will add up to this macro feeling

00:06:42.240 --> 00:06:43.620
in the marketplace over time.

00:06:43.620 --> 00:06:46.380
But what's modern now might
not feel modern in five,

00:06:46.380 --> 00:06:49.410
or 10 more years from
now, but the Kia logo

00:06:49.410 --> 00:06:53.646
is built off simple design
principles, so that will endure.

00:06:53.646 --> 00:06:56.813
(bright upbeat music)

